  "texts": [
    "Water boils calmly, so why does milk suddenly boil over?",
    "Milk is about 87 percent plain water.",
    "But it also holds proteins, fat and milk sugar.",
    "As it heats, some proteins unfold and clump together.",
    "On the surface they form a thin, stretchy skin.",
    "Near boiling, steam bubbles form at the hot bottom.",
    "In plain water, bubbles reach the top and simply pop.",
    "In milk, though, the skin traps them underneath.",
    "Proteins and fat also coat each bubble, making it sturdy.",
    "So bubbles pile up on each other into thick foam.",
    "Steam keeps coming, and the foam rises in seconds.",
    "It climbs over the rim and spills onto the stove.",
    "Tip: turn down the heat and stir to break the skin.",
    "And a wider pot gives bubbles more room to burst.",
    "Follow for more, your kitchen is full of physics!"
  ]
